Z||000000||GeeDee86GT||12-10-2000||10:18 AM||||This has probably been done before, but the forum is growing by leaps and bounds. Are there any Fiero (or not) e-zines or club newsletters we should be reading for their quality and content??  I realize we would have to join a specific club for their newsletter.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/garby_d/siggy.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||rodmcneill||12-10-2000||12:07 PM||||Good question! I have been a member in 3 different clubs and I always looked forward to the club magazine arriving. I have noticed a lack of technical info. in some of them but part of the problem is members not sending in articles. When I bought my first Fiero about 3 years the previous owner included a lot of older club magazines. A lot of these clubs are no longer around but the magazines have a lot really good technical info. In the magazines I am now receiving If I read one more article on how the Fiero was born I will puke! I realize that new members are joining all the time and they might interested in this but for older members give us some "meat and potatoes" articles that we can actually use. Since I have come on this Forum I have really enjoyed the tech. questions and feedback from the members.||||reg||10
